Kia ora Charles,

I tested your four PRs (Seeed #284, #286 and #289, and ww-hardware #77) on
the bench. With both chips on the new firmware, normal wakes were clean: no
errors over 35 wakes, photo times right, the new threshold matches the PC,
and photos download faster.

Two problems block merging:

   - After a wake without a restart, the AI chip answers the self-test
   before it has checked the SD card, so a missing card is reported as fine
   (your Seeed #290). Your lorawanPing branch fixes this, so I'd like it to go
   in with the rest. When it's finished, could you open PRs for it in both
   repos, with the Bluetooth version set to 0.30.62?
   - Seeed #296
   <https://github.com/wildlifeai/Seeed_Grove_Vision_AI_Module_V2/issues/296>,
   the himax chip says "Sleep", then spends a few seconds on its clock before
   it really goes to sleep. This messes up with the BLE chip and mobile app.

Meanwhile, a FYI I've:

   - Updated the mobile app (ww-mobile-app #527). A camera with only one
   chip updated can't receive files from the app, so the app won't offer the
   Bluetooth update until the AI chip has been updated.
   - Taken your own build of 0.30.60 out of ww-hardware #77, put back the
   older images it deleted, set the version to 0.30.61, and had CI build it
   on your branch. 0.30.60 already names your test builds, so we skip it.
   Please pull before you commit to that branch again.
   - Updated the mobile app for your threshold and bit 15 changes.

I've also raised Seeed #295 for the photo date: please leave the date out
when the camera doesn't know the time. And I've parked #247 and #288.

On your question about bit 14: it needs to stay set because the message
that would report it is the one that failed. One question back: the
Bluetooth chip overwrites the AI chip's error bits at every wake, so bit 14
only reaches the app if a phone connects before the next wake. Should the
Bluetooth chip hold it until the mobile app has read it?

Once your PRs are open, I'll bench them and merge all six together.

Stay in touch,

*Dr Victor Anton* | General Manager

[image: wildlife.ai] <http://wildlife.ai>

Watch our 1-minute video. <https://youtu.be/VQCgUqeNSsU?si=lkFMAMobQF-oDxlh>

